      "body": "\n**What.** `fused_gdn_gating_kernel` allocates `beta_output` as an fp32 buffer, but stores\n`sigmoid(b)` narrowed to the *input* dtype:\n\n```python\n# python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/fla/fused_gdn_gating.py\nblk_beta_output = tl.sigmoid(blk_b.to(tl.float32))\ntl.store(beta_output + off, blk_beta_output.to(b.dtype.element_ty), mask=mask)\n```\n\nNo bf16 arithmetic happens between the fp32 sigmoid and the narrowing, so the round-trip only\ndiscards the low mantissa bits — up to bf16 epsilon (~0.39%) per value — and the fp32 buffer\nends up holding bf16-precision contents.\n\n**Why it matters.** That tensor is what the extend path feeds into the delta-rule update of the\npersistent SSM state (`gdn_backend.py`, `kernel_dispatcher.extend(beta=beta, ...)`); the same\ntensor is used by the non-packed decode path and by the NPU backend\n(`hardware_backend/npu/attention/ascend_gdn_backend.py`). `beta` scales the state on every step,\nand the state is read, scaled and written back each token, so the rounding is not a one-off loss.\n\n**Fix.** Store the fp32 value into the fp32 buffer:\n\n```python\ntl.store(beta_output + off, blk_beta_output, mask=mask)\n```\n\n**Relationship to #38977 (do not duplicate).** #38977 fixes a *different* pair of sites —\nthe sigmoid expression itself in `fused_recurrent.py` (GDN packed decode) and\n`fused_recurrent_linear_replayssm.py` (KDA replay decode), both of which narrow the sigmoid\nbefore it is used at all. This change is on the gating kernel, which computes the gate for the\nextend/prefill path and stores it for another kernel to consume. The two are independent: they\ntouch different files and different code paths, and either can land without the other. Same\nunderlying defect class, same origin as vllm-project/vllm#53877.\n\n**Test.** `test/registered/unit/layers/attention/test_gdn_gating_beta_fp32.py` — a CPU source\nguard (the kernel needs a GPU, so the guard is a scan of the kernel source) plus a CPU\ndemonstration of the error class: a bf16 round-trip of `sigmoid` has max relative error ~3.8e-3,\nwell above fp32 noise. Verified red→green: the store check fails on the pre-fix source and\npasses after.\n\n```\n$ python -m pytest test/registered/unit/layers/attention/test_gdn_gating_beta_fp32.py -q\n3 passed\n```\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35550495718](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35550495718)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35550495539](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35550495539)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35550495664](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35550495664)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
